            <ArticleTitle>[The MDR3 gene mutation: a rare cause of progressive familial intrahepatic cholestasis (PFIC)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>581-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 47-year old man complained about persistant pain and cholestasis 12-years after a cholescystectomy. In his family, all his brothers and sisters had cholecystectomy. Genetic explorations revealed a MDR3 gene mutation. All symptoms disappeared with a treatment by ursodesoxycholic acid. MDR3 gene mutation is to be researched in all cases of familial cholestasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
